    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0740" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg647"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3831/123: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-20T11:00:00-05:00">February 20, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Personal for Edwin Wilson. Referring to Department’s instruction No. 262,
                    February l.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d655-f1"/> Haitian Government advises me today
                    they will accept trade agreement as drafted with the exception of article 9025,
                    schedule I,<anchor n="15" xml:id="d655-f2"/> which they ask be stricken out.</p>
                <p>In view of Haitian Government’s acceptance reduction butter and milk products, de
                    la Rue feels that you will probably be willing to make this small concession. He
                    is writing a full personal explanation to you by air mail tomorrow. It is
                    expected instructions will be sent Blanchet by same mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d655-f1" n="14" xml:id="d655-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d655-f2" n="15" xml:id="d655-f2-content">
                <p>This article provided for hides and skins.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
